===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þrír}}, from {{inh|is|gmq-pro|ᚦᚱᛁᛃᛟᛉ|tr=þrijoz}} {{qualifier|feminine plural}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þrīz}}, ultimately from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*tréyes}}. Compare Faroese {{m|fo|tríggir}}, Norwegian, Swedish, and Danish {{m|da|tre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θriːr/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|iːr|lang=is}}

===Numeral===
'''þrír''' {{g|m-p}}, '''[[þrjár]]''' {{g|f-p}}, '''[[þrjú]]''' {{g|n-p}}

# [[three]]; the cardinal number after {{m|is|tveir||two}} and before {{m|is|fjórir||four}}.

